# Git commits — no co-authors

Never add `Co-authored-by:` or `Co-Authored-By:` trailers to commit messages, PR descriptions, or squash-merge bodies.

- Commits must list only the human author (`git config user.name` / `user.email`).
- Do not attribute Cursor, Claude, Copilot, hawk, or any AI tool as a co-author.
- If a commit template or tool suggests a co-author trailer, omit it.

Example — do **not** append:

```
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```
